    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0103" n="1063" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1063"/>

                <head>No. 733.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hubbard to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tokio</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-12-28"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 28, 1887</date>.
                        (Received January 21, 1888.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 419.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose for the
                    information of the State Department two copies of a late Imperial rescript
                    promulgated on the 25th instant, intended, as expressed by the Government, to
                    secure “the maintenance of public tranquility and to prevent disturbances
                    opposed to the welfare of the people and to the nation’s political reforms.”</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard B.
                    Hubbard.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d20-a1.xml" xpointer="d20-a1"/>
            </div>
